    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101701" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφιγκ-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tight-bound</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of the person bound, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.229
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.), <i><span class="en">
				9.641
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the
			thing that binds, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. στεφάνων ἀμφὶ κόμαισι
				μίτος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.174
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. μόρος</span> death <i>by
				strangling</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				3.590
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἐπίδεσμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paul.Aeg.
					6.99
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1424.49
				</span></i>
			: neut. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφιγκτά</span> as
				Adv., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.272
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pers.
			</span></i>).</div>
